[{"id":5158092113,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM3I9UQ","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"3e0c4f3962ac9d38354e7fa18100c3a2af780fde","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","login":"kitbdev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev"},"body":"Tested, fixes the issue.\nI don't know if its valid to call `initialize_class` like this, needs core review.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123332#pullrequestreview-5158092113","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123332","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-09T18:06:38Z"},{"id":5158303684,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM3V3xA","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"3e0c4f3962ac9d38354e7fa18100c3a2af780fde","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Yea, this is fine.\n\nA class is normally initialized when it is explicitly registered (e.g. `GDREGISTER_CLASS`), or when it is instantiated.\n\nThis code needs neither, and it would be odd to do it. \nWorth noting that `initialize_class` is commented with \"should be protected\", but I think this is a design mistake. Calling it directly is the best way to ensure the class has finalized if you don't want to do either of the previous two.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123332#pullrequestreview-5158303684","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123332","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-09-09T18:29:12Z"},{"id":5180951864,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNM8NOA","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"3e0c4f3962ac9d38354e7fa18100c3a2af780fde","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","login":"Repiteo","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo"},"body":"This probably warrants a more elegant solution in the future for these bound test classes, but this should suffice for now","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123332#pullrequestreview-5180951864","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123332","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-11T16:17:01Z"}]